#X text 82 694 0: signal left \; 1: signal right \; 2: events: value \, dump, f 64;
#X obj 60 770 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Messages 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 794 <pitch> <velocity> \, note <p> <v>: note on/off (0 = off) \; <p> <v> <channel>: from [notein] \, filtered by ch1 \; <control> <0-127>: set a control by name \, e.g. har1 64 \; ctl <index> <0-127> \, params v0 v1 ...: set by index \; <setting> <value>: e.g. cut 60 (see Settings below) \; bend <-1..1>: pitch bend of all voices (master clock) \; defaults \, reset: default values \, reset also stops all voices \; panic: all voices off \; get <name>: reply 'value <name> <v>' on outlet 2 \; print: voices \, values and sample rate to the Pd window \; dump: send all values to outlet 2 as 'dump pdoly8 v0 ..' \; dump pdoly8 v0 v1 ...: restore such a dump (this voice only) \; voice <i> <p> \, voiceoff <i>: play one voice directly, f 64;
#X obj 60 1030 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Controls\ (index\ name\ default) 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1054 0 har1 (45) Timbre of DCO1 \, one knob through all 15 distinct \; original timbres \, dark to bright: 0 16' / 9-64 saw net (16'2' \, \; 16'4'2' \, 16'4' \, 16'8'4' \, all at 45 \, 16'8'2' \, 16'8') / 73-127 \; square net (16'8' \, 16'8'4' \, 16'4' \, 16'4'2' \, all \, 16'8'2' \, \; 16'2'). One foot or the net per step \, no jumps. Combinations \; without 16' = oct1 2-4. \; 1 har2 (45) Timbre of DCO2 \, same path. \; 2 env1 (0) Envelope of DCO1 (DEG1) \, one knob: 0 gate / 1 very \; short pluck (no fade from the gate) / 24 pluck / 48 piano / 72 \; long release / 92 swell / 108 pad / 127 long pad. -1 = own \; values a1 ... r1. \; 3 env2 (0) Envelope of DCO2 (DEG2) \, same\; -1 = own values a2 \; ... r2. \; 4 intv (0) Interval of DCO2 above DCO1 \, 0-12 semitones. \; 5 detn (0) Detune of DCO2 downwards: the original's 4 steps 0 \, \; 6.5 \, 13 \, 26 cents lie at 0 \, 42 \, 85 \, 127. \; 6 lev1 (127) Level of DCO1. \; 7 lev2 (0) Level of DCO2 (every voice has both DCOs). Above \; full scale (lev1 + lev2 > 127) both are scaled down together., f 64;
#X obj 60 1386 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Settings\ (name\ default) 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1410 oct1 \, oct2 (0) octave -1 0 1 (LOW MID HIGH) \, 2-4 feet shifted \; nois (0) white noise level 0-15 \, sounds while a voice sounds \; sprd (0) stereo spread of the 4 voices 0-127 \; mrph (8) smoothing of har and lev changes in ms \; bnd (2) pitch bend range in semitones (original: up to 7) \; mgf (5) MG rate in Hz\; mgr (-1) the same in steps 0-15 \; mgi (0) vibrato depth in cents (original: 12.4 per step) \; hsnp (1) plateau around each foot combination \, in har steps \; ch1 (0) MIDI channel for p v ch lists \, 0 = any \; tone (1) 1: output response measured on a Poly-800 with the \; VCF (54 Hz high-pass \, VCF \, 1 pole at 5 kHz) \, 0: raw \; pw1 \, pw2 (64) pulse width of DCO1 / DCO2: 0-127 = 3-97 % \, \; 64 = square\; works on every foot at once (see PWM) \; sync (0) 1: DCO2 restarts at every period of DCO1 \; fm (0) 0-127: FM index of DCO1 \, 0-8 (through zero above 45) \; fmr (1) FM ratio of the sine modulator to DCO1 \, 0.125-16 \; fms (0) FM source: 0 internal sine \, 1 DCO2 (cross FM) \; wsh1 \, wsh2 (0) Walsh loop position of DCO1 / DCO2 \, 0-127 \; wmx1 \, wmx2 (0) mix from the feet (0) to the Walsh loop (127) \; leak (0) 1: released voices stay at -55 dB \, as on the original \; a1 d1 bp1 sl1 su1 r1 (0 0 31 0 31 0) DEG1 attack \, decay \, \; break point \, slope \, sustain \, release 0-31 (env1 becomes -1) \; a2 d2 bp2 sl2 su2 r2: the same for DEG2 \; port (0) portamento 0-127 = off to 3 s (not on the Poly-800) \; pmod (0) glide from: 0 the last note \, 1 the voice's own last \; note \, 2 the last note only while another key is held \; cut (99) VCF cutoff 0-99 (66 Hz - 20 kHz \, 4 poles \, measured) \; res (0) resonance 0-15 (no self-oscillation \, as the original) \; kbd (0) key tracking 0 off \, 1 half (ref C6) \, 2 full (ref C4) \; pol (2) DEG3 polarity 2 up \, 1 down\; egi (0) EG INT 0-15 \; trg (2) DEG3 trigger 1 single \, 2 multi \; env3 (0) DEG3 morph (VCF and noise) \, -1 = own a3 ... r3 \; a3 d3 bp3 sl3 su3 r3: DEG3 values 0-31 \; mgd (0) MG delay 0-15 (0.47 s at 5 / 1.55 s at 15) \; mgv (0) MG to VCF 0-15 (+-7.9 octaves at 15) \; treb bass (0 0) EQ -6..6 = -10..+10 dB (2 kHz / 300 Hz) \; dtim (30) delay time 0-99 = 4-1024 ms\; dfb (0) feedback 0-15 \; dmf dmi (0 0) delay mod rate 0-31 = 0.1-10 Hz and depth 0-31 \; dlev (0) delay effect level 0-15 (0 = off), f 64;
#X obj 60 2062 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty How\ the\ Poly-800\ makes\ its\ sound 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 2086 One master clock feeds the MSM5232: 8 tone generators in two \; groups (TG0-3 = DCO1 \, TG4-7 = DCO2). Each key becomes an \; integer divider from the chip's ROM \, then a binary counter \; whose bits are the 16' \, 8' \, 4' and 2' squares \, locked in \; phase. The four feet of a group are summed to a square or a \; step saw. Bend and vibrato move the master clock \, so \; all voices move together. Detune thins out DCO2's clock. \; Every edge is band-limited: analog edges \, no aliasing., f 64;
#X obj 60 2242 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Timbre\ (har1\ /\ har2) 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 2266 The 15 distinct timbres of the original \, dark to bright: \; 0: 16' / saw net 9: 16'2' / 18: 16'4'2' / 27: 16'4' / \; 36: 16'8'4' / 45: all / 54: 16'8'2' / 64: 16'8' / \; square net 73: 16'8' / 82: 16'8'4' / 91: 16'4' / \; 100: 16'4'2' / 109: all / 118: 16'8'2' / 127: 16'2'. \; One foot or the net per step. The combinations without 16' \; are the same waves higher: use oct1 / oct2 2-4. \; A fading foot rises in power \, so the morph has no dips., f 64;
#X obj 60 2422 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty PWM 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 2446 pw1 / pw2 turn every foot into a pulse: the AND of the foot \; with a copy shifted by part of its period \, so the falling \; edge stays on the counter step and the rising edge moves. \; On the saw net this gives pulse staircases. All edges stay \; band-limited., f 64;
#X obj 60 2554 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Sync\ and\ FM 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 2578 sync 1: DCO2's counter restarts at every 16' period of DCO1 \, \; at the exact sub-sample time. Step DCO2 with intv or oct2 \; for the classic sync sound\; lev1 0 to hear DCO2 alone. \; fm: linear FM of DCO1's counter rate by a sine at fmr times \; its 16' frequency (fms 0) or by DCO2 (fms 1). Above index 1 \; the counter runs backwards for a moment (through zero) \, so \; integer ratios stay harmonic. All edges stay band-limited., f 64;
#X obj 60 2718 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Walsh\ morph 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 2742 The feet are Rademacher functions\; their products (XOR of \; the foot squares) are the 15 Walsh functions: two-level waves \; whose energy sits around harmonic 1 ... 8 of the 16'. wsh \; moves along a closed loop of them by sequency \, up through \; one of each pair and down through the other\; neighbours fade \; at equal power \, so the level stays. 0: 16' / 8: 8' / \; 17: 16'x4' / 25: 4' / 34: 16'x4'x2' / 42: 8'x2' / 51: 16'x2' / \; 59: 2' / 68: 16'x8'x2' / 76: 8'x4'x2' / 85: all / 93: 4'x2' / \; 102: 16'x8'x4' / 110: 8'x4' / 119: 16'x8' / 127 = 0. \; wmx fades from the feet sum to the Walsh loop., f 64;
#X obj 60 2930 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty VCF\ and\ DEG3 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 2954 One 4-pole VCF for the instrument \, as the NJM2069 \, measured \; on a Poly-800: cutoff 0-99 = 66 Hz ... 20 kHz (13 steps per \; octave) \, resonance an uncompensated ladder (bass falls as it \; rises \, no self-oscillation). DEG3 (one \, paraphonic) moves the \; cutoff by up to 7.9 octaves (EG INT 15) and sets the noise \; level \, both linear in its level. Single trigger: only the \; first key starts DEG3\; multi: every key. Full tracking follows \; the highest key 1:1 (C4 nominal) \, half by 1/2 (C6 nominal)., f 64;
#X obj 60 3110 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Envelopes\ (DEG1\ /\ DEG2) 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 3134 Each tone generator has its own 6-stage DEG as on the \; Poly-800 (attack \, decay \, break point \, slope \, sustain \, release \; 0-31) \, measured on a real one: level 0-31 is about (L/31)^2 \, \; attack rises linearly (A31 about 9 s) \, decay \, slope and \; release fall at a constant dB per second (31: about 18 s \; to -40 dB). env1 / env2 / env3 morph through settings: \; 0 gate / 1 short pluck / 24 pluck / 48 piano / 72 long rel. / \; 92 swell / 108 pad / 127 long pad. Always 4 voices of \; DCO1 + DCO2\; lev1 / lev2 set the mix., f 64;
#X obj 60 3306 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Presets\ and\ steps 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 3330 Per-step values: connect the voice to [skpreset name] \; (outlet 2 -> inlet 0 \, outlet 0 -> voice inlet). A slot \; number 0-15 then recalls and keeps the values for a step. \; More in skpreset-help.pd (click to open)., f 64;
#X msg 82 3404 dir;
